    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0739" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/993: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Counselor of Embassy in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Chungking</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-21T16:00:00-05:00">February 21, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Your 81, February 19, 9 a.m., extra-Settlement roads. It is suggested that,
                    as in the case mentioned in your 300, May 1, 3 p.m., 1939<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d786-f1"/> (Chinese activities in International Settlement), the
                    Embassy make acknowledgement to the Foreign Office to the effect that the matter
                    has been referred to the Department.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
